program	errors/ref_field_type.saw
triple	arm64-apple-darwin
twin	same
expect	error
build	refused	Parse error at 12:20: field `r` of `Holder` may not be a reference: its type `&Int` is a reference, and references in Saw are PARAMETERS ONLY — a reference borrows storage for the duration of one call and may not escape it (designs 88/106; the Law of Exclusivity is statically sound only because every live reference belongs to a call still on the stack). A field outlives every call that could have created the reference, so the pointer it holds outlives the storage it names. Store the value instead (`r: Int`), or — to hand out storage this type already owns — declare a `borrows` accessor (`... borrows -> &var Int` with `lend`, design 141), which lends the place for a window rather than letting a pointer out. To hold a lent place for the extent of ONE window, declare the type `borrows struct Holder` (design 275 U3): a borrowing struct's values live only inside their window, which is what makes the shared field sound
meets_expect	yes
log	"error: Parse error at 12:20: field `r` of `Holder` may not be a reference: its type `&Int` is a reference, and references in Saw are PARAMETERS ONLY — a reference borrows storage for the duration of one call and may not escape it (designs 88/106; the Law of Exclusivity is statically sound only because every live reference belongs to a call still on the stack). A field outlives every call that could have created the reference, so the pointer it holds outlives the storage it names. Store the value instead (`r: Int`), or — to hand out storage this type already owns — declare a `borrows` accessor (`... borrows -> &var Int` with `lend`, design 141), which lends the place for a window rather than letting a pointer out. To hold a lent place for the extent of ONE window, declare the type `borrows struct Holder` (design 275 U3): a borrowing struct's values live only inside their window, which is what makes the shared field sound"
